---
# A rule this plugin gives every project that declares it. `uze <plugin>@<market>`
# copies it, byte for byte, into that project's `.agents/rules/`, where the
# project commits it and every harness reads it.
#
# trigger: when it reaches an agent.
#   always_on       every session, from its start: how a plugin speaks to every
#                   agent of a declaring project
#   glob            when an agent reads or edits a path `globs` matches
#   model_decision  when the task fits `description`, which says when to read it
#   manual          only when someone names it
trigger: glob
# Comma-separated patterns, matched against paths relative to the root of the
# project that declares the plugin. Each opens with `**/` or holds no `/`
# (`*.md` matches at any depth); `*`, `**`, `?` and `[...]` are supported.
# Quoted, since YAML reads a value opening with `*` as an alias.
globs: "**/*.md"
---
Write documentation in sentence case, one sentence per line.
